  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0095_22e1dcbbcaf5.png\" style=\"width: 295px; height: 170px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>When first pulse is applied the potential across capacitor is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>When no pulse is applied, capacitor will discharge like&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;when again, second pulse is applied&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Using all three equations the correct graph is :</p>"
  }
